parameters.text:
=You are a writer. Using ONLY the research notes below, write a friendly, well-structured article of about 500 words for an audience of {{ $('Article Brief Form').item.json.Audience }} on "{{ $('Article Brief Form').item.json.Topic }}". Use short paragraphs and a clear intro and conclusion. Do not invent facts beyond the notes.

Research notes:
{{ $json.output }}

=You are an SEO editor. Improve the draft below: tighten the writing, fix any awkward phrasing, and naturally work in the keyword "{{ $('Article Brief Form').item.json.Keyword }}" where it fits. Then output the finished article, a compelling 55-60 character SEO title on a line starting "TITLE:", and a 150-character meta description on a line starting "META:".

Draft:
{{ $json.text }}

parameters.jsCode:
const out = String($json.text || '');
const t = out.match(/TITLE:\s*(.*)$/im);
const m = out.match(/META:\s*(.*)$/im);
const title = t ? t[1].trim() : '';
const meta = m ? m[1].trim() : '';
const body = out.replace(/TITLE:\s*.*$/im, '').replace(/META:\s*.*$/im, '').trim();
const f = $('Article Brief Form').item.json;
return { email: f['Your email'], topic: f.Topic, title: title, meta: meta, article: body };

parameters.message:
